mainmenu "SmartKnob"
source "Kconfig.zephyr"
config SK_PRESS_THRESHOLD
    int "HX711 press threshold in raw ADC counts"
    default 50000
    range 100 8000000
config SK_MOTOR_DEADTIME_NS
    int "Motor gate dead time in nanoseconds"
    default 500
    range 250 1500
config SK_MOTOR_SUPPLY_MV
    int "Motor driver supply voltage in millivolts"
    default 5000
    range 3000 12000
    help
      Supply assumed by voltage-mode FOC when converting requested phase
      voltages to PWM duty. The Dev Kit drives the TMC6300 from USB 5 V.
config SK_MOTOR_CALIBRATION_MV
    int "Calibration alignment vector in millivolts"
    default 2000
    range 500 3000
    help
      d-axis voltage used to drag the rotor during calibration. Too little
      lets cogging and friction stop the rotor; the simulation in
      tests/motor_sim.c calibrates reliably from 2 V. No current sensing:
      the stall current is roughly this voltage over the phase resistance.
config SK_ENCODER_LOSS_POLICY
    int "MT6701 tracking-loss frame policy"
    default 1
    range 0 2
    help
      0: reject every CRC-valid frame that flags loss of tracking.
      1: accept it while its angle continues the last accepted angle and a
         clean frame arrived within the last 200 ms.
      2: accept it while its angle continues the last accepted angle; the
         factory firmware ignores the flag entirely.
      Rejected frames always turn the gates off for that period.
config SK_MOTOR_CONTINUOUS_MV
    int "Highest sustained motor voltage in millivolts (0 disables)"
    default 1500
    range 0 2500
    help
      Without current sensing the firmware estimates winding heating from
      the applied voltage (V^2, 4 s time constant). When it exceeds this
      rating, haptic torque tapers down to it, so holding an end stop at
      full force cannot heat the motor indefinitely. Clicks and press
      pulses are too short to trigger it; it recovers when the knob rests.
